       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose.\n\n- **Maximum dose:** The limit is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Extended-release is capped at 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This dose would greatly raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), or\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll note the reason on the order."
